<Popup Visible="@Visible" VisibleChanged="@OnVisibleChamged" Title="Symptom Help">
    <h2>Symptoms</h2>
    <p>
        Symptoms are the physical or mental health effects your health problems cause you. When you create a symptom you do not need
        to write about how it is effecting you today as that will be in your symptom reports (see below). Instead write a summary of the overall
        effects on your health. Changes to your symptoms are logged over time for you to view later.
    </p>
    <h2>Symptom Reports</h2>
    <p>
        Symptom reports are where you can write about how each symptom is effecting you specifically today, you will be asked to mark the
        severity of the symptoms out of 10 and you can also write some notes to refer to later. This will allow you to build a profile of your
        health and symptoms over time.
    </p>
    <p>
        Reports can be created for symptoms by pressing the <span class="material-symbols-outlined">article</span> button next to your symptom
        name and description. If needed you can change the date and time on the report so that you can log historic reports if you forget to
        do them. 
    </p>
</Popup>

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool Visible { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> VisibleChanged { get; set; }

    private async Task OnVisibleChamged(bool visible)
    {
        await VisibleChanged.InvokeAsync(visible);
    }
}
